              057e:2009/2017/200e device that does not answer
              JC_USB_CMD_HANDSHAKE on the first try but would have
              probed successfully at the default baud rate under
              vanilla's fallback -- PR #92 now sends it
              JC_USB_CMD_BAUDRATE_3M and a second, fatal handshake it
              was never going to answer either, so probe fails where
              vanilla succeeded. Confirmed against vanilla 6.18.49 and
              the fork's refs/pr/92 diff directly (not inferred) --
              orchestrator finding, code-review 2026-09-11, reproduced
              independently in this patch's own authoring session by
              diffing the pre-0049 (eight-patch) tree against PR #92's
              diff applied on top. THIS patch keeps PR #92's intent
              (read_info before baudrate; skip baudrate/handshake
              entirely for the 8BitDo OUI) but restores vanilla's
              fallback with one added local: `bool usb_handshook =
              false;`, set true only inside the first handshake's
              success body (`hid_dbg(hdev, "detected USB controller\n");
