              read_info unconditionally, then the baudrate block gated
              on `if (usb_handshook && !joycon_device_is_8bitdo(ctlr))`
              -- so a USB device that never answered the first
              handshake gets neither the 8BitDo carve-out nor a second,
              fatal handshake attempt; it falls through exactly as
              vanilla does.
